        "nobel_worthiness": "Dynamical mean-field theory made a broad class of strongly correlated electron problems quantitatively tractable and became a central tool for understanding real materials.",
        "attribution": "Georges, Vollhardt, and Kotliar are central contributors to the method's formulation and development; the wider community's extensions make precise credit worth examining.",
        "maturity": "A mature framework with decades of successful use and continuing contact with experimental materials research.",
        "uncertainties": [
