      "assessment": {
        "nobel_worthiness": "The quantum spin Hall effect and time-reversal-invariant topological insulators established a major new class of quantum materials and quantized edge transport.",
        "attribution": "Kane and Mele supplied the key theoretical prediction, while Molenkamp's experiments demonstrated the quantum spin Hall state; the later three-dimensional topological-insulator work widened the field.",
        "maturity": "The early predictions and observations are well established, with a large body of later work confirming and extending the materials platform.",
        "uncertainties": [
