      "assessment": {
        "nobel_worthiness": "Spin-orbit torques showed how electrical currents can manipulate magnetization, adding a useful and physically rich mechanism to spintronics.",
        "attribution": "Miron, Gambardella, and Buhrman are prominent contributors to the experimental discovery and understanding of interfacial and spin Hall torque mechanisms.",
        "maturity": "The effect is established across many materials, although device approaches and the relative importance of different mechanisms continue to evolve.",
        "uncertainties": [
          "The discovery comprises several related torque mechanisms and competing microscopic explanations.",
          "The distinction between fundamental discovery and technological development is not yet as clear as for older landmark results."
        ]
      }
    },
